      "id": 1,
      "options": {
        "content": "## SR Policy Observability Overview\nThis dashboard summarizes the current bounded SR policy slice exposed by the platform. It focuses on real Prometheus-backed evidence: collector policy ingestion health, backend policy snapshot readiness, live-empty policy context, bounded static-policy detail when present, persisted policy sync evidence, and API demand around the policy view.\n\nCurrent limits:\n- The live policy slice still starts with Nokia SR policy counters and only adds bounded static-policy observations where that state is actually exposed.\n- A zero-policy view can still be healthy; live-empty state is explicit and should not be confused with a placeholder response.\n- Observed policy counts and detailed policy record counts are intentionally separated because the bounded read path cannot yet derive per-policy detail for every observed type.\n- Persisted policy sync evidence now exists, but richer per-policy validation history and drift history still do not.\n- Grafana remains observability-only. Policy exploration and future action flows stay in the WebUI and backend.",
        "mode": "markdown"
      },
      "pluginVersion": "11.0.0",
      "title": "Dashboard Scope",
      "type": "text"
    },
